Topology:
PC0 -- SW0 -- R0 -- R1 -- SW1 -- PC1

PC0:
IP 192.168.1.10
Mask 255.255.255.0
Gateway 192.168.1.1

R0 LAN:
192.168.1.1/24

R0-R1:
R0 = 10.0.0.1/30
R1 = 10.0.0.2/30

R1 LAN:
192.168.2.1/24

PC1:
IP 192.168.2.10
Mask 255.255.255.0
Gateway 192.168.2.1

STATIC ROUTES

R0:
ip route 192.168.2.0 255.255.255.0 10.0.0.2

R1:
ip route 192.168.1.0 255.255.255.0 10.0.0.1

RIP VERSION 2

router rip
version 2
network 192.168.1.0
network 10.0.0.0
no auto-summary

On R1 use its LAN network:
network 192.168.2.0
network 10.0.0.0
no auto-summary

Verify:
show ip route
show ip protocols
ping 192.168.2.10
Compile / Run:
Use Cisco Packet Tracer.
Sample Output:
R0# show ip route
R 192.168.2.0/24 [120/1] via 10.0.0.2

PC0> ping 192.168.2.10
Success rate is 100 percent (4/4)
